<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>go-slides – Math</title><link>https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.16/tags/math/</link><description>Recent content in Math on go-slides</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.16/tags/math/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Math and code</title><link>https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.16/math-and-code/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.16/math-and-code/</guid><description>
&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-2 hx:ltr:pr-4 hx:rtl:pl-4 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-amber-200 hx:bg-amber-100 hx:text-amber-900 hx:dark:border-amber-200/30 hx:dark:bg-amber-900/30 hx:dark:text-amber-200"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:ltr:pl-3 hx:ltr:pr-2 hx:rtl:pr-3 hx:rtl:pl-2"&gt;&lt;svg height=1.2em class="hx:inline-block hx:align-middle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;Math and code are in v0.2.0.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="math"&gt;Math&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="math"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#math" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;$…$&lt;/code&gt; is an inline formula and &lt;code&gt;$$…$$&lt;/code&gt; a display formula:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;The famous one is $E=mc^2$, and this is a display formula:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;$$
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;\int_0^\infty e^{-x^2}\,dx = \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;$$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The delimiter rules are Marp Core&amp;rsquo;s, read from marp-core 4.4.0: a &lt;code&gt;$&lt;/code&gt;
followed by a space does not open a formula, and one followed by a digit
does not close it, so prices such as &lt;code&gt;$5 and $10&lt;/code&gt; stay text.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-tex/math" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-tex/math&lt;/a&gt; typesets each formula into
inline SVG sized in &lt;code&gt;em&lt;/code&gt;, so it follows the text&amp;rsquo;s size and sits on its
baseline. The same SVG is used in the HTML page, in images and in the PDF.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A formula that does not parse stays visible as written; the error is kept in
its &lt;code&gt;title&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="code"&gt;Code&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="code"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#code" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fenced code blocks are coloured by &lt;a href="https://github.com/go-rouge/rouge" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-rouge&lt;/a&gt;,
which writes highlight.js class names, the ones Marp&amp;rsquo;s themes style:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;Println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;hello&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A language go-rouge does not know is written as plain text, as Marp Core does.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="line-numbers"&gt;Line numbers&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="line-numbers"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#line-numbers" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;In v0.8.0 a block can number its lines. Marp Core has no line numbers, and
it ignores what follows a fence&amp;rsquo;s language, so the options go in braces there
and a deck that uses them renders in Marp as it would without:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;``&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`go {lineNumbers}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;func main() {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;hello&amp;#34;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;`&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;`&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`go {lineNumbers=10}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;// starts at 10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;``&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Write&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Means&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;{lineNumbers}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;number from 1 (Slidev&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;{lines:true}&lt;/code&gt; and Pandoc&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;{.numberLines}&lt;/code&gt; are read too)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;{lineNumbers=10}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;number from 10 (also &lt;code&gt;startLine=10&lt;/code&gt;, Pandoc&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;startFrom=&amp;quot;10&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;{lineNumbers=false}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;no numbers, whatever the slide says&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For every block of a slide and the slides after it, set the directive:
&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;!-- lineNumbers: true --&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;_lineNumbers&lt;/code&gt; for one slide). A kind can set it
once for a family of slides:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;kinds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;listing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;{&lt;span class="nt"&gt;lineNumbers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each number starts its line inside the theme&amp;rsquo;s code box, set apart by a rule.
It stays on its line&amp;rsquo;s baseline even when the line is taller, for example
with a callout or an emoji. The numbers are muted by a colour mixed from the
code&amp;rsquo;s colour and its background, with 4.5:1 contrast or more in the default,
gaia and uncover themes, light and dark. They are &lt;strong&gt;not selectable&lt;/strong&gt; in the
page and are not read by screen readers. In a PDF they are drawn but left out
of the text, so a text extractor reads the code alone. In a PowerPoint or
OpenDocument file they are editable text at the start of each line. A deck
that does not use the option renders as before, to the byte. Highlighting
chosen lines is not supported yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="code-callouts"&gt;Code callouts&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="code-callouts"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#code-callouts" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;In v0.8.0 a code line can end with a numbered disc that refers to a note
below the block. The syntax is
&lt;a href="https://quarto.org/docs/authoring/code-annotation.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Quarto&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/a&gt;, which is
also Asciidoctor&amp;rsquo;s comment form. The marker is a comment in the code&amp;rsquo;s own
language, so the code stays valid, and the notes are the ordered list right
after the block:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;load&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// &amp;lt;2&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;Println&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt; The entry point.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;2. Reads the input.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Write&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Means&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;// &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;# &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;-- &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;; &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;% &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;' &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a line comment that holds only the marker: both are replaced by the disc&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;!-- &amp;lt;1&amp;gt; --&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/* &amp;lt;1&amp;gt; */&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the same, for languages with wrapped comments&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;// &amp;lt;1&amp;gt; &amp;lt;2&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;two discs on one line&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;x = 1 # count &amp;lt;1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the comment&amp;rsquo;s text stays and the disc follows it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The markers become discs only when the list right after the block starts at 1
and has an item for every number. Otherwise the block stays as written. The
discs are rings in the code&amp;rsquo;s colour, in the default, gaia and uncover themes,
light or dark. The list&amp;rsquo;s items are numbered with the same discs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The discs are &lt;strong&gt;not selectable&lt;/strong&gt;. Copying the code from the page gives the code
without its markers. In a PDF they are vectors left out of the text, and in a
PowerPoint or OpenDocument file they are editable shapes. Callouts combine
with line numbers. Marp Core has no callouts (marp-core 4.4.0), so in Marp the
comments and the numbered list show as written. A deck that does not use them
renders as before, to the byte.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In v0.9.0, a disc and its note find each other in the HTML page. Hovering a
disc, or reaching it with Tab, tints its note, and a note does the same for its
disc. This is what Quarto&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;code-annotations: hover&lt;/code&gt; does, but here the style
sheet does it alone, with no script. It therefore works the same in the
playground&amp;rsquo;s sandboxed preview and in VS Code&amp;rsquo;s preview, which both restrict
scripts. Each disc is described by its note, so a screen reader reads the note
when it reaches the disc. The tint fades in only when the reader has not asked
for reduced motion. Images, PDF, PowerPoint and OpenDocument files are
unchanged, byte for byte.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="fonts"&gt;Fonts&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="fonts"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#fonts" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lato Regular, Bold, Black and italics and Roboto Mono Regular, Bold and
italics are embedded, so gaia&amp;rsquo;s headings get their weight and italic text
renders italic.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>